WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.341
Private investing is inherently unstructured.

00:00:02.341 --> 00:00:09.386
Data comes from different sources in different formats, and a lot of analysts' time is spent just structuring it.

00:00:09.386 --> 00:00:13.604
In the operational flow of a VC, there are different phases.

00:00:13.604 --> 00:00:21.493
In pre-screening alone, analysts spend hours on repetitive tasks just to screen every pitch that comes in each month.

00:00:21.493 --> 00:00:26.201
What we've built is an AI analyst that solves the pre-call intelligence layer.

00:00:26.201 --> 00:00:29.870
It takes data from the sources the fund already uses.

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.648
Let's say a deck comes in.

00:00:31.648 --> 00:00:33.976
The key information is extracted.

00:00:33.976 --> 00:00:36.177
The claims inside it are verified.

00:00:36.177 --> 00:00:39.133
And the data is enriched from external sources.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:44.077
And all of this happens inside the tools the fund already uses.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:53.562
On Slack, in a brief that gives you the full pre-call picture with a score, and the CRM or the Google Sheet is updated automatically.

00:00:53.562 --> 00:00:58.446
You can also interact with every deck the fund has received over time.

00:00:58.446 --> 00:01:03.218
This becomes a persistent context, personalized to how that fund invests.

00:01:03.218 --> 00:01:10.317
As these operations get automated, a context graph is built underneath — the institutional memory for private investors.

00:01:10.317 --> 00:01:11.892
We are Hizen.

00:01:11.892 --> 00:01:15.569
We are building the intelligence layer for private investing.
